 594               /CLOCK ROUTINE FOR THE KW12A - THE 'HESITATE' COMMAND
 595               
 596               /START WITH 'H -5,Q' WHERE Q IS THE TIME IN UNITS OF 0.01
 597               /SECONDS.  THUS Q=100 IS A 1 SECOND COUNTING PERIOD.  TO
 598               /CHOOSE OTHER UNITS, CHANGE THE FIRST PARAMETER (WHICH MUST
 599               /BE NEGATIVE) TO SELECT A DIFFERENT TIME BASE.  THUS -4 =
 600               /0.001 SECONDS (MILLISECONDS) AND -6 = RATE DETERMINED BY
 601               /INPUT #1.  (SEE THE LABORATORY COMPUTER HANDBOOK.)
 602               
 603               /IT IS NOT NECESSARY TO SET THE UNITS UNLESS YOU WISH TO
 604               /CHANGE IT FROM 0.001 SECONDS, BUT IF YOU DO YOU MUST GIVE
 605               /A NEW DELAY COUNT TOO. (DELAY MUST BE LESS THAN 4096.)
 606               /'H' THEN WAITS UNTIL THE END OF THE NEXT COUNTING CYCLE.
 607               
 608               /TO RING THE BELL OF THE TTY EVERY 4 SECONDS:
 609               
 610               /       1.1 H 4000;C OR: H -5,400
 611               /       1.2 H FOUT(135);L B 1.2;R
 612               
 613               /FOR ANOTHER APPROACH SEE DECUSCOPE 14 #2 P.27 (1975)
 614               
